{{!
    @template minilessonitem_smartframe/smartframe

    A widget item. The iframe has no src here: the item's JS sets it once it is listening for the widget's
    messages, so the widget's first message can not be missed.

    The sandbox lets the widget run scripts and keep its own origin (it needs both to load its files and
    to talk to the lesson). That is only safe because widgets are served from a separate widget host,
    never from Moodle. allow-forms is there because a form submit in a sandbox without it is dropped
    before the submit event, which breaks widgets that handle submit in JS.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "uniqueid": "item1",
        "widgeturl": "https://widgets.example.net/0123/index.html?lang=en&parentOrigin=https%3A%2F%2Fschool.example.org",
        "widgettitle": "Greetings"
    }
}}
{{> mod_minilesson/questionheader}}
<div class="minilessonitem_smartframe_widget">
    {{#widgeturl}}
        <iframe class="minilessonitem_smartframe_frame"
                title="{{widgettitle}}"
                sandbox="allow-scripts allow-same-origin allow-forms"
                referrerpolicy="no-referrer"
                loading="lazy"
                style="display:block;width:100%;height:360px;border:0;"></iframe>
    {{/widgeturl}}
    {{^widgeturl}}
        <div class="alert alert-info">{{#str}}widgetnotavailable, minilessonitem_smartframe{{/str}}</div>
    {{/widgeturl}}
</div>
{{> mod_minilesson/questionfooter}}
